WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.380
Plenty of actors have starred in&nbsp;
movies or TV shows that most people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.496
don't know about — but who ever&nbsp;
knew that Cameron Boyce did this?

00:00:08.496 --> 00:00:12.900
The late Cameron Boyce once starred in&nbsp;
a movie back in 2008 that his fans have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.924
likely forgotten about — especially those&nbsp;
who know him for his family-friendly work.

00:00:16.924 --> 00:00:22.440
Boyce, who died in 2019, is most well-known for&nbsp;
his performances in a handful of Disney Channel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:27.900
shows and movies that were released throughout the&nbsp;
2010s. Boyce began to earn some early attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.840
in 2011 when he landed the recurring role of&nbsp;
Luke Ross on the Debby Ryan-led series Jessie.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.040
Boyce's fame continued to grow in&nbsp;
2015 when he appeared as Carlos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.780
the son of Cruella de Vil, in the Disney&nbsp;
Channel original movie Descendants. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.584
went on to reprise his role as Carlos&nbsp;
in three more Descendants movies.

00:00:46.584 --> 00:00:48.744
Outside of his work for the Disney Channel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.744 --> 00:00:53.760
Boyce also had notable recurring roles on&nbsp;
the HBO original series Mrs. Fletcher and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.860
Amazon Prime musical TV show Paradise City.&nbsp;
Long before he appeared in those TV shows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.240
however, Boyce made his big-screen&nbsp;
debut in a now-forgotten horror movie.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:09.540
In 2008, Cameron Boyce starred as a young boy&nbsp;
named Michael in Alexandre Aja's supernatural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:14.160
horror film, Mirrors. The film follows a&nbsp;
former cop as he and his family are targeted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:19.302
by a malevolent force that is attempting to use&nbsp;
mirrors to make its way into the physical world.

00:01:19.405 --> 00:01:20.845
"We gotta get going, okay?"

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.660
"Okay."

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:28.320
A remake of a 2003 South Korean&nbsp;
horror movie titled Into the Mirror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.360
this movie wasn't particularly well received by&nbsp;
critics or casual viewers when it was initially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.460
released in 2008. While the movie managed to&nbsp;
more than double its $35 million production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:44.820
budget at the box office, it currently boasts&nbsp;
a low 15% Tomatometer score on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:50.820
The film's audience score sits slightly higher at&nbsp;
44%, but that isn't high enough to earn Mirrors a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:55.708
"Fresh" rating. In his review of the film for&nbsp;
Entertainment Weekly, Owen Gleiberman wrote:

00:01:55.708 --> 00:02:00.088
"The director, Alexandre Aja, knows how&nbsp;
to reflect the fear in people's heads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.624
but he gets too ensnared in a backstory&nbsp;
that's just gothic business as usual."

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:10.020
However, in his write-up of the movie for Reel&nbsp;
Film Reviews, David Nusair actually praised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.269
Mirrors, observing that it is, quote, "often far&nbsp;
more entertaining than it has any right to be."

00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:19.560
Notably, Mirrors marked Boyce's first&nbsp;
and only horror movie. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:25.200
it's quite clear that the film's poor reception&nbsp;
hasn't tainted Boyce's legacy in any tangible way.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:31.440
At just 20 years old, Boyce died from epilepsy in&nbsp;
2019, cutting short his burgeoning screen career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.760
Boyce turned in his final screen performance&nbsp;
as Simon in the first season of Paradise City,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.160
which premiered on Amazon nearly two full years&nbsp;
after his death. But despite the fact that Boyce's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:47.040
career ended in 2019, his legacy continues to live&nbsp;
on. In fact, many of the actors and collaborators&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.180
with whom he worked over the years have been&nbsp;
consistently willing to sing his praises;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.260
many have spoken openly about the positive&nbsp;
experiences that they shared with him.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:59.700
Following Boyce's tragic death, several&nbsp;
of his most notable co-stars took to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:03.180
social media to pay tribute to him.&nbsp;
Adam Sandler, for instance, tweeted:

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:06.643
"Too young. Too sweet. Too funny. Just the nicest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.643 --> 00:03:09.960
most talented, and most decent kid&nbsp;
around. [...] Thank you, Cameron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.580
for all you gave to us. So much more was&nbsp;
on the way. All our hearts are broken."

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:19.560
In addition to Sandler, several of Boyce's&nbsp;
Disney Channel collaborators were also quick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.480
to publicly pay their own tributes. Three years&nbsp;
after his death, Boyce's Descendants co-star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.601
Sofia Carson, even took a moment to&nbsp;
remember him, writing on Instagram:

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:32.198
"Three years without you. I love&nbsp;
you, forever. I miss you, forever."

00:03:32.198 --> 00:03:37.080
Carson's post proves that, among other things,&nbsp;
the death of Boyce continues to be felt deeply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:42.840
by both his fans and loved ones. And while Boyce&nbsp;
will no doubt be missed, there's no denying that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:48.120
he left behind an impressive assortment of movie&nbsp;
and TV performances that his fans can continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:53.280
to enjoy for many years to come — including&nbsp;
his supporting turn as Michael in Mirrors.

